(ENV-03: `first` (LANGUAGE.md:4567) is documented as the full
 "NAME=value" string. Scan its bytes for `=` to confirm the shape,
 vacuously true on an empty environment (`first` returns an empty
 string with no error there -- confirmed separately). NOTE: this reads
 `environment's first` into a `text` first, THEN declares a buffer from
 that text -- declaring a buffer directly from `environment's first`
 is broken (empty content, size -1) -- see Discrepancy 1, D1.vox.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox ENV-03.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   well-formed: contains =
)
